{"_v":1,"id":"hairspray-2002","cat":"broadway","bd":{"positive":6,"mixed":0,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":89,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2002/legit/reviews/hairspray-12-1200546769/","d":"2002-08-16","q":"He’s effortlessly adorable — and so, for that matter, is the show."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"About Entertainment","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"d":"2002-08-16","q":"IF life were everything it should be — that is, if life were more like the endearing new musical called ”Hairspray” that opened last night at the Theater — your every waking thought would be footnoted by a chorus of backup singers of early 60’s vintage."},{"cn":"Linda Winer","o":"Newsday","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/190143076/","d":"2002-08-16","q":"In such a moment, \"Hairspray,\" which opened Thursday night after enough hype to power a nuclear sub, lifts the $10.5-million adaptation of John Waters' bad-taste, good-values 1988 cult film into the must-see zone of transcendence."},{"cn":"Howard Kissel","o":"New York Daily News","s":86,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/408386823/","d":"2002-08-16","q":"With this role, Fierstein places himself in the great line of Broadway divas."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":85,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.talkinbroadway.com/world/Hairspray.html","d":"2002-08-15","q":"Right now, Hairspray is a joyous tribute to an era past, and an intelligent, warm, and joyous musical comedy of the type Broadway should never be without."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"TheaterMania","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.theatermania.com/news/hairspray_2474/","d":"2002-08-15","q":"Yes: No matter what misgivings a reviewer may have, Hairspray holds."}],"au":{"score":88.69,"designation":"Loving","sources":{"ss":{"s":89,"c":767},"mz":{"s":88,"c":345,"sr":4.4}}},"tn":[{"yr":57,"cat":"Best Musical","n":null,"w":true},{"yr":57,"cat":"Best Book of a Musical","n":"Mark O'Donn